Abstract = {Historically, fault injection was the realm of adversaries with physical
   access. This changed when research revealed that remote attackers could
   use software to inject faults. Plundervolt is a new software-based
   attack on Intel's trusted execution technology (SGX). Plundervolt can
   break cryptography and inject memory-safety bugs into secure code.},
