   Grenoble, FRANCE, MAR 09-13, 2020},
Abstract = {Compliance testing for RISC-V is very important. Therefore, an official
   hand-written compliance test-suite is being actively developed. However,
   this requires significant manual effort in particular to achieve a high
   test coverage.
   In this paper we propose a test-suite specification mechanism in
   combination with a first set of instruction constraints and coverage
   requirements for the base RISC-V ISA. In addition, we present an
   automated method to generate a test-suite that satisfies the
   specification. Our evaluation demonstrates the effectiveness and
   potential of our method.},
