Number = {1},
Month = {JAN 1},
Abstract = {Using the density functional theory, energetics and electronic
   structures of single walled carbon nanotube (CNT) encapsulated in boron
   nitride nanotube (BNNT) are investigated. Cohesive energy of CNT inside
   BNNT depends on the spacing between them and on their mutual
   arrangement. Band gap of CNT encapsulated in BNNT is modulated by about
   tens of meV, when they have AB stacking arrangement where B atoms are
   located as close as to C atoms, indicating that BNNTeffectively affects
   the tensile strain onto CNT. Carrier accumulation into CNToccurs under
   external electric field, where BNNT acts as the gate insulator
   surrounding CNT. (C) 2019 The Japan Society of Applied Physics.},
