Note = {Latin American Electron Devices Conference (LAEDC), San Jose, COSTA
   RICA, FEB 25-28, 2020},
Abstract = {Algorithm is the way of performing any task in a correct way to reach
   desired goal. Algorithm is very important factor in any digital world.
   In digital world, is complicated to implement arithmetical operations.
   Arithmetic and logical unit stands to be a very vital unit of any
   embedded or digital processors. Following Moore's Law density of logic
   units has increased tremendously over couple of decades, which provides
   enough availability of resources to implement all arithmetic operations.
   Amongst addition, subtraction, multiplication and division, division is
   the toughest one to implement digitally. Till date, many different
   algorithms were developed to provide better result to division
   implementation in digital hardware. Generally, the major aspects that
   must be considered are quotient convergence rate, hardware primitives,
   overheads, and mathematical formulation. Usually division algorithms
   have five different classes and several types. Many practical dividers
   are made up of hybrid class concept. In today's high-speed digital life,
   it is important to implement correct division. This paper is focused on
   the study of different algorithms to understand how they work, which
   their limitations are and how it is possible to improve them and the
   possibility of developing new division algorithms.},
