   ELECTR NETWORK, NOV 02-05, 2020},
Abstract = {Exciting times in hardware design are upon us. Spear-headed by the
   RISC-V ISA, and the recent DARPA POSH/IDEA program which focuses on both
   open source IP and open source CAD, a large number of open source HW
   projects are underway. Academics are increasingly releasing their code
   online. Many agile open source HW projects envision a hypothetical user
   that may not actually exist. To acquire real users, we must be pragmatic
   about what kinds of systems our HW will go into and focus on the
   roadblocks unique to those systems.},
