   Communications (ICDIPC), Avrasya Univ, Trabzon, TURKEY, MAY 02-04, 2019},
Abstract = {The concern of portability in designs brought more importance to the
   power consumption aspect. Hence, works on power consumption prediction
   and reduction in complex digital designs becoming even more prominent.
   Nowadays, similiarly popular softcore processor designs, along with lots
   of useful trairts, becoming resourceful test units for these sorts of
   research. Thus, in this work; one of the softcore processors is
   examined, some power consumption tests were applied on its
   post-implementation model and problems that could be encountered during
   installation are listed with their solutions, in order to be a reference
   for further works. Also, a technique for creating momentary power
   consumption profile, a concept that has importance in terms of side
   channel analysis of cryptographic algorithms during design stage, was
   specified and used on aforementioned processor.},
