Abstract = {This paper presents a new design for SoC clocking based on open-loop
   frequency multiplication. The architecture, fully implemented in 28nm
   FD-SOI standard cells, achieves frequency tracking within one input
   reference period making it a promising candidate for Dynamic Voltage and
   Frequency Scaling (DVFS) schemes. A calibration scheme is implemented
   for wide voltage range (0.6-1.2V) operation and to offset P\&R and
   variability induced mismatch. Measurements at 0.6V (0.8/0.4V FBB) show a
   Fmax of 93MHz with a power of 2.91mW/MHz and a jitter of 2.7 \% UI.},
