   16-19, 2015},
Abstract = {This work demonstrates a RISC-V vector microprocessor implemented in
   28nm FDSOI with fully-integrated non-interleaved switched-capacitor DCDC
   (SC-DCDC) converters and adaptive clocking that generates four on-chip
   voltages between 0.5V and 1V using only 1.0V core and 1.8V IO voltage
   inputs. The design pushes the capabilities of dynamic voltage scaling by
   enabling fast transitions (20ns), simple packaging (no off-chip
   passives), low area overhead (16\%), high conversion efficiency
   (80-86\%), and high energy efficiency (26.2 DP GFLOPS/W) for mobile
   devices.},
